{"item_id": "feed:https://www.rokslide.com/rifle-elk-hunting-201-finding-bulls-everyone-else-misses-with-cody-rich/", "version_id": "fd883cc77012eb63bc0995a89951b78c2478f9435d10a57093fb36c6074f04df", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under the Relevance section, this podcast covers hunting tactics, habitat, and elk-finding strategy rather than gear, which the policy explicitly rejects as hunting tactics and game content. Its only gear-adjacent mention is passing anecdote, so it does not help a competitor decide what to carry.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://www.rokslide.com/tract-toric-lrf-rangefinding-binocular-review/", "version_id": "220ed6eb0893442944fab61d7dad5202a7be74c9abe5e6d3b342f9fc0db3d2a2", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Under Relevance, this is a spotting and measuring gear review (rangefinding binocular with ballistic solver), and under Credibility the reviewer describes hands-on field use, cold-soak and drop testing, and a side-by-side elk hunt against a Leica Geovid Max with measured range agreement within 2 yards, which is stronger than spec-sheet restatement. Under Commercial incentives, the publisher is ad-supported and the reviewer's praise comes from a single reviewer, with no sponsorship disclosed for this product; the 'Tract Trust Assurance' warranty mention and Eagle Ballistics partnership are noted but not treated as independent confirmation, and the reviewer notes long-term durability is untested. Best supports Piece 02 (claims tested against independent measurement, including the wind-direction and laser-alignment claims) and Piece 03 (practical implications for ranging and ballistic use), and the Mammoth connection is that the device targets long-range elk-style ranging conditions. Mammoth official requirements are not in evidence and are not asserted.", "piece_ids": ["02", "03"]}
{"item_id": "feed:https://www.rokslide.com/gear-reviews-lathrop-super-wides-peak-refuel-kuiu-icon-6-and-patagonia-nano-air/", "version_id": "7ef51cb374c67132a3da0a97951a46f030fe892a8095fa3fc0ebd8821faee971", "decision": "defer", "reason": "This is a podcast roundup of four products (Peak Refuel meals, KUIU Icon 6, Patagonia Nano-Air, Lathrop Super Wides) where the discussion is mostly interview-based and does not supply measured field data; the in-scope gear is covered only at a summary level. Under Credibility and Uncertainty, the evidence is too thin to rely on yet, and the Icon 6 is better handled by its dedicated full review, so defer rather than duplicate.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://www.rokslide.com/stories-from-western-hunting-legend-jim-zumbo/", "version_id": "2d7ee6911a3933d9a2a30d38b3c5d8c25d1f0916da9bf7808a4f4000856e3642", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under Relevance, this interview is historical hunting stories and tactics (still-hunting, fair-chase ethics, mule deer and sheep hunts) with no gear evaluation, and the policy rejects hunting tactics and game content. It offers no new product information for competitors.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://www.rokslide.com/kuiu-icon-6-3500-backpack-review/", "version_id": "e05dabe7e03e73aeb70fd9c735e547f1271e3a12c4896b1ef987af9b31254b57", "decision": "accept", "reason": "Under Relevance, this is a rucking and endurance pack review, and the policy specifically values load-carrying durability and comfort on foot. Under Credibility, the reviewer measured performance with a described test (1.2-mile loops at 510 vertical feet with 28 lb day load and an added 64 lb simulated elk quarter, compared against Stone Glacier and Kifaru packs), and reported weight measured on the reviewer's scale; the reviewer is ad-supported and the publisher's ad relationship is noted, but no specific sponsorship of KUIU is disclosed in the item. Its claims about the frame's durability and damage tolerance are manufacturer-stated and are not independently confirmed here, and the 'bargain' and 'premium' framing is opinion. Best supports Piece 02 (manufacturer frame claims tested against practitioner loads) and Piece 03 (practical load-carry implications), with the caveat that the Icon 6's incompatibility with earlier Icons is a relevant tradeoff for readers.", "piece_ids": ["02", "03"]}
{"item_id": "feed:https://www.rokslide.com/how-ai-is-helping-hunters-score-bucks-faster-and-smarter/", "version_id": "77fdb2e910eed2a4c81a023a3c002f87bd7d3cf15d0d6a32a5a08fd1787dc190", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under Relevance, the episode is mainly about a scoring app for trophy estimation and includes a tripod discussion, but the scoring app is not competitor gear for Mammoth, and the tripod content is a brief sponsor-linked segment with no test data; the Vizirack app is a hunting-trophy tool outside the in-scope categories, and the Altitude Outdoors segment is promotional. Under Commercial incentives, the Altitude Outdoors and Vizirack segments are host-introduced sponsor features, and the policy treats sales and promotional content without substantive evidence as rejectable.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://kitbadger.com/1st-look-parish-optics-infitac-salt-of-the-earth/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=1st-look-parish-optics-infitac-salt-of-the-earth", "version_id": "fdb0ec4afc0ac636d14515558283887d9319e7cc2cc93d8ebc5e1c3efb3c1c29", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under Relevance, the item is a short first-look promotional post with no substantive testing or field data for the Parish PVS31 night vision, Infitac thermal, or hydration salts, and under Commercial incentives it reads as sponsored promotional content. The policy rejects sales, deals, and promotional posts with no substantive content, so it does not meet the evidence threshold for acceptance or deferral.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://soldiersystems.net/2026/10/15/springfield-armory-announces-launch-of-echelon-pro-9mm-pistols/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=springfield-armory-announces-launch-of-echelon-pro-9mm-pistols", "version_id": "3817723344efb197629cd7aea2da202413b1fc7e5fcf57cf6283d1671fcaeb1e", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under Exclusions, this is a review-free manufacturer press release for a firearm (a 9mm pistol), and reviews of firearms are excluded. It is also a commercial press release with no independent evidence, so it fails Relevance and Credibility.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://soldiersystems.net/2026/10/15/reptilia-introduces-q-sert-versions-of-torch-light-body-and-socket-qd-sling-mount/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=reptilia-introduces-q-sert-versions-of-torch-light-body-and-socket-qd-sling-mount", "version_id": "3c0f1fd2620d88baadd3520b225c95a1af7458be0979a8409253568c4ecb60ab", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under Relevance, this is a manufacturer press release for weapon-mounted accessories (Q-Sert handguard lights and sling mounts) that are not in the policy's in-scope gear categories and are tied to firearm handguards. Under Commercial incentives and Credibility, it is an advertiser announcement with no independent testing, so it provides no evidence for competitor decisions.", "piece_ids": []}
{"item_id": "feed:https://soldiersystems.net/2026/10/15/army-hosts-international-signing-ceremony-for-uas-and-counter-uas-marketplaces-at-ausa-2026/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=army-hosts-international-signing-ceremony-for-uas-and-counter-uas-marketplaces-at-ausa-2026", "version_id": "111fd9afec5b36a2ce1f292d4e3459830d2a9d12a45082702214c53d576512d6", "decision": "reject", "reason": "Under Relevance, this is a U.S. Army procurement and diplomacy story about UAS and counter-UAS marketplaces, which falls outside every in-scope gear category and is unconnected to Mammoth competitor gear. It contains no product evaluation or practitioner evidence.", "piece_ids": []}
